{
  "server": {
    "name": "community-weavatrix-refactor-js",
    "command": [
      "npx",
      "-y",
      "weavatrix-refactor-js"
    ],
    "container_command": [
      "weavatrix-refactor-js-mcp"
    ],
    "version": "weavatrix-refactor-js 0.3.15 (npm latest at image build time)",
    "note": "Drawn in frame order at position 59 of Frame 3; re-entered under amendment 9.8 (its declared binary is weavatrix-refactor-js-mcp). Forty five tools, none annotated. Source edits are enabled by the documented WEAVATRIX_ALLOW_SOURCE_EDITS=1. A server prelude opens a seeded one-file git repository; open_repo is not under test. Its graph cache lives under HOME and is not observed; the repository is observed with .git excluded.",
    "env": {
      "HOME": "{root}/home",
      "NO_COLOR": "1",
      "WEAVATRIX_ALLOW_SOURCE_EDITS": "1"
    },
    "prelude": [
      [
        "open_repo",
        {
          "path": "{root}/repo"
        }
      ]
    ],
    "observer": {
      "kind": "filesystem",
      "path": "",
      "ignore": [
        "home",
        "home/*",
        ".DS_Store",
        "repo/.git",
        "repo/.git/*"
      ]
    },
    "setup": {
      "directories": [
        "home"
      ],
      "git": {
        "path": "repo"
      },
      "files": {
        "repo/app.js": "export function alpha() {\n  return 1;\n}\n\nexport function beta() {\n  return 2;\n}\n",
        "repo/package.json": "{\"name\":\"demo\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"type\":\"module\"}\n"
      }
    },
    "timeout_s": 150.0,
    "image": "agent-fault-lab:reprobe-bin-n2"
  },
  "fixtures": [
    {
      "tool": "edit_symbol",
      "id": "insert_after_symbol",
      "arguments": {
        "symbol": "app.js#alpha@1",
        "operation": "insert_after_symbol",
        "content": "\nexport function gamma() {\n  return 3;\n}\n"
      },
      "probes": [
        [
          "read_source",
          {
            "path": "app.js",
            "start_line": 1,
            "before": 0,
            "after": 40
          }
        ]
      ],
      "note": "Inserts a new function after alpha. The symbol is passed by its graph node id, since the bare name is not resolved."
    },
    {
      "tool": "edit_symbol",
      "id": "replace_symbol_body",
      "arguments": {
        "symbol": "app.js#beta@5",
        "operation": "replace_symbol_body",
        "content": "export function beta() {\n  return 22;\n}"
      },
      "probes": [
        [
          "read_source",
          {
            "path": "app.js",
            "start_line": 1,
            "before": 0,
            "after": 40
          }
        ]
      ],
      "note": "Replaces beta's definition."
    },
    {
      "tool": "apply_edit_plan",
      "id": "apply_insert_after_symbol",
      "arguments": {
        "plan": "{plan}",
        "mode": "apply",
        "confirm_token": "{token}",
        "output_format": "json"
      },
      "prelude": [
        [
          "edit_symbol",
          {
            "symbol": "app.js#alpha@1",
            "operation": "insert_after_symbol",
            "content": "\nexport function gamma() {\n  return 3;\n}\n",
            "output_format": "json"
          },
          {
            "plan": "result.plan"
          }
        ],
        [
          "apply_edit_plan",
          {
            "plan": "{plan}",
            "mode": "preview",
            "output_format": "json"
          },
          {
            "token": "result.confirmToken"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "fault_occurrence": 2,
      "probes": [
        [
          "read_source",
          {
            "path": "app.js",
            "start_line": 1,
            "before": 0,
            "after": 40
          }
        ]
      ],
      "note": "The plan comes from edit_symbol and the single-use confirm token from apply_edit_plan in preview mode, both in the fixture prelude; the apply call is the second call of apply_edit_plan in each trial, so the fault is aimed at occurrence 2. Both applications and the retry reuse the one token."
    },
    {
      "tool": "apply_edit_plan",
      "id": "apply_replace_symbol_body",
      "arguments": {
        "plan": "{plan}",
        "mode": "apply",
        "confirm_token": "{token}",
        "output_format": "json"
      },
      "prelude": [
        [
          "edit_symbol",
          {
            "symbol": "app.js#beta@5",
            "operation": "replace_symbol_body",
            "content": "export function beta() {\n  return 22;\n}",
            "output_format": "json"
          },
          {
            "plan": "result.plan"
          }
        ],
        [
          "apply_edit_plan",
          {
            "plan": "{plan}",
            "mode": "preview",
            "output_format": "json"
          },
          {
            "token": "result.confirmToken"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "fault_occurrence": 2,
      "probes": [
        [
          "read_source",
          {
            "path": "app.js",
            "start_line": 1,
            "before": 0,
            "after": 40
          }
        ]
      ],
      "note": "The plan comes from edit_symbol and the single-use confirm token from apply_edit_plan in preview mode, both in the fixture prelude; the apply call is the second call of apply_edit_plan in each trial, so the fault is aimed at occurrence 2. Both applications and the retry reuse the one token."
    }
  ]
}
